{
    "word": "umbilicus",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                "word": "umbilicus",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a0a50ed4-d4a6-4a19-aa12-7a2f38ac348a",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "umbilici"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b6f2440a-93ea-462c-bd82-0df26a8f8f67",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "umbilicuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "92542556-fd74-3dfb-bdba-bd0917aa8d9f",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "navel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "993c6407-918b-3631-823d-5a16cbac1643",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Umbilical cord"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "proscribed",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdcfeac7-6440-4509-89d2-d72567b95a29",
                                "sense_id": "993c6407-918b-3631-823d-5a16cbac1643",
                                "text": "Although I have been tempted to cut the umbilicus, and pass a ligature round the remaining portion on one occasion, yet I now deem such interference officious and uncalled - for at this eventful period."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "edb09fb2-8a4b-471e-92a8-cbd63f3d62ff",
                                "sense_id": "993c6407-918b-3631-823d-5a16cbac1643",
                                "text": "She ate the umbilicus, and the afterbirth, which is supposed to be good for them. Then she licked off the first kitten and was ready for the next."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35b91337-f2d3-4363-a5c2-d4e362558698",
                                "sense_id": "993c6407-918b-3631-823d-5a16cbac1643",
                                "text": "Then he tied the umbilicus in two places, using bits of Manila twine, and made his cut between them."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34418650-662b-34f1-aec4-e1dff6dbf8bb",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "hilum"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba802d0e-ee74-3f31-8149-74f3dcd7e82d",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A depression or opening in the center of the base of many spiral shells."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4a0757e-610f-32fc-933b-901163378b2f",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Either of the two apertures in the calamus of a feather."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2cbb42b-99d0-36ee-a505-37b3fcbcde55",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tube connecting an astronaut or spacecraft to the mothership, through which supplies and samples can be transferred."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9664585-3f91-46c6-aa64-6e35e6decf27",
                                "sense_id": "f2cbb42b-99d0-36ee-a505-37b3fcbcde55",
                                "text": "The importance of the visual analyzer is further increased when the cosmonaut is in free space with only the slight support of an umbilicus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d5a0888-6726-4c24-901e-cbae873bac05",
                                "sense_id": "f2cbb42b-99d0-36ee-a505-37b3fcbcde55",
                                "text": "Penetrators will be connected by an umbilicus to an afterbody containing imaging and meteorological instruments."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "584a8640-0c6a-4d03-ac3c-a258cb6b72e2",
                                "sense_id": "f2cbb42b-99d0-36ee-a505-37b3fcbcde55",
                                "text": "How about a 270 mile tether to an orbiting satellite? Oh, you'd like that, wouldn't you? Frank! Prepare to receive the umbilicus!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc4e7898-466c-4c1a-9cc2-ba1da39b0f58",
                                "sense_id": "f2cbb42b-99d0-36ee-a505-37b3fcbcde55",
                                "text": "Ninety minutes into the twenty-six hour flight, Leonov opened the outer hatch and pushed himself out to the end of his 17-foot umbilicus — becoming the first man to walk in space."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fafbf6dc-5e2a-37a5-9d85-6468a819c444",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of the foci of an ellipse or other curve."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58cf2dba-781d-3f79-9b6a-220d404324c4",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A point of a surface at which the curvatures of the normal sections are all equal to each other."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8bdd713-852b-4c86-9ffe-2f323dcb3e1f",
                                "sense_id": "58cf2dba-781d-3f79-9b6a-220d404324c4",
                                "text": "A sphere may be osculatory to the surface in every direction at an umbilicus."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c39b740-8bb5-3164-8060-c0ff2a2604dc",
                        "entry_id": "aa46315f-111e-34cd-8677-95a69b9d5425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ornamented or painted ball or boss fastened at each end of the stick on which manuscripts were rolled."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72a34a4f-4ec9-47c4-b587-c47a016fdf8f",
                                "sense_id": "3c39b740-8bb5-3164-8060-c0ff2a2604dc",
                                "text": "The ends of the umbilicus were called cornua (i.e. horns) in Latin, and were usually adorned with some pretty device"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
